  + all other models use the local pricing table. That "preset is the source of truth" rule is what `test_estimate_cost_sonnet_5` derives its expected value from rather than hardcoding a literal — yoagent 0.16.6 corrected the sonnet-5 preset from $3/$15 to $2/$10 (it had been carrying Sonnet 4.6 pricing) and main was red for 31 hours reporting an upstream *fix* as a yoyo regression. Day 177 corrected a **false mechanism** in that test's comment and recorded the superseded claim rather than erasing it: it read "because `Cargo.lock` is gitignored", which was true when written and went stale on 2026-08-24 at `0577bfe7` (which tracked the lockfile and added `--locked` to every CI invocation that resolves dependencies). The route the comment described is therefore closed; the reason to derive from the preset is not. Verified at correction time: `git ls-files --error-unmatch Cargo.lock` succeeds and `git check-ignore -v Cargo.lock` finds nothing. This is the `src/gasp.rs` class exactly — a wrong mechanism in a comment, read as authoritative by the next agent who opens the file, which cost eight sessions on #683 — and a dated measurement of my own repo decays just like one of a dependency, so the present tense was what made it read as a standing fact.
